1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:06,260
Hello, and welcome to Acquired, the podcast about great companies and the stories and playbooks behind them.

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,280
I'm Ben Gilbert.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,700
I'm David Rosenthal.

4
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:10,260
And we are your hosts.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:18,780
So, Ben and I are obsessed with uncovering the history, strategy, and stories behind what built the greatest companies in the world.

6
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:25,640
Each month, we choose a company, and we spend the entire month researching what uniquely made it work, where many others failed.

7
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:34,080
The output of that is a full-day recording session where Ben and I come together and tell the absolute deepest business and technology stories on the internet.

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:41,000
And when we say obsessed, we mean that we spend 100 hours each reading everything that exists about a company,

9
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:45,600
and doing primary research and background interviews with the people who lived it firsthand.

10
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:52,420
These are stories like NVIDIA, Costco, Hermes, Microsoft, Rolex, Amazon.

11
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:54,580
Those are some of our favorites, anyway.

12
00:00:54,580 --> 00:01:05,040
What started 10 years ago as just the study of tech companies has led to a curiosity about our broader world from Berkshire Hathaway to the NFL or even Taylor Swift.

13
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:10,640
Our goal in creating each episode is to uncover the secrets that are lurking in plain sight

14
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:14,820
and how these world-changing companies went from obscurity to ubiquity.

15
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:19,660
So if you've ever wondered, how did Starbucks end up on every corner around the globe?

16
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:25,700
Or what does Visa actually do, and how did they become the payment rails of the whole globe?

17
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:29,700
Or why is the NFL so much bigger than other sports leagues?

18
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,380
Then Acquired is for you.

19
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,180
Yep.

20
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,520
We have a unique format that we do on the show.

21
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,800
We call it a conversational audiobook.

22
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:41,680
Ben and I tell these stories of these companies through a deep conversation.

23
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:45,180
And typically, it's just the two of us without an interview guest.

24
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:50,180
Occasionally, we will bring in a protagonist from the story, like Howard Schultz from Starbucks,

25
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,000
or Jensen Huang from NVIDIA, or Mark Zuckerberg from Meta.

26
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:57,680
Usually, though, that's as a follow-up interview to a deep dive that we've already done on their company.

27
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,660
Now, one thing we should say.

28
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:05,940
Our episodes are typically very long, like three to four hours long, since we go really deep.

29
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:06,880
But don't be scared.

30
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,340
These are amazing stories that deserve every minute.

31
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:13,160
And we have a lot of fun along the way.

32
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:19,240
Our goal is really to deliver a complete understanding of a company by the time you finish the episode.

33
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,820
So we're glad you're here.

34
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,260
Welcome.

35
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:29,520
And if you ever want to discuss any episodes or give us any feedback, join us in the Acquired community at Acquired.fm slash Slack.

36
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,400
Welcome.

37
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:30,580
Welcome.
